    "result_text": "All 9 test classes ran \u2014 **17 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp09Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for `POST /api/owners`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Domain & persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be in the schema script).\n- `db/hsqldb/data.sql` \u2014 the seed rows use column-less `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, so I appended a `NULL` for the new column to each. (The other DBs use explicit column lists and needed no change.)\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions.\n\n**Request pipeline (OfficeFloor function injection)**\n- New `rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 reads the built `Owner` via `@Val`, computes `LAST3` (upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`) and `NNNN` as `String.format(\"%04d\", ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1)`, and mutates the entity in place.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignCustomerCode` step between `build` and `save` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`), so the new owner isn't yet counted when its sequence is assigned, giving the global \"one more than current owner count\" behavior the spec and test require.\n\nThe `Cp09Tests` assertion (SMI-/JON- prefixes and a sequence that increments by exactly one between successive creates) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
